### [the shaft](shaft)
---
Relic: voice
Box: 600, -1600, 0, 380, 1400, 380
---
Straight down from the concourse. On a top-down plan a vertical shaft is a dot - read the
second number.

### [the transmitter bay](bay)
---
Relic: voice
Box: 600, -3000, 0, 1000, 500, 1000
---
The dead heart. Whatever the Torgoth built the rest of this station around, they built it
around this room.

### [the cradle](cradle_solid)
---
Relic: voice
Solid: box, 600, -3000, 0, 320, 200, 320
---
A subtracted mass in the middle of the bay - the machine's own mounting block, hanging in
the room you have to fly around it in.

### [the fallen span](span_solid)
---
Relic: voice
Solid: capsule, -1100, -300, -700, -100, 300, 700, 160
---
A structural spar down across the concourse. It has been there a long time.

DIAGONAL, and it stops short of the walls. Squared off across the room it spanned the
whole width and left a 240u slot at each end - an accidental chokepoint the plan view
does not show you, because a solid reads as a hole rather than as a wall. Set on the
diagonal it is something to fly around, which is what it is for.

### [the mouth](mouth)
---
Relic: voice
Point: -4700, 0, 0
Roles: entrance
---
The way in, and what your sensors see first. `Roles: entrance` is what puts a contact
here on arrival and what Storm's briefing measures its range against.

### [the concourse marker](at_concourse)
---
Relic: voice
Point: -1200, 0, 600
Roles: voice_concourse
---
A named place is a quest target: a chamber the story wants to react to gets a point with
a role, and a beat reaches for it. Nothing else is needed.

Off the room's centre on purpose - the fallen span runs through the middle of it, and a
marker inside a subtracted mass is a place no ship can ever reach.

