### [the core cradle](core_place)
---
Relic: voice
Point: 1300, -3000, 0
Roles: voice_core, relic_piece
Item: beacon_voice
---
Where the transmitter core sits. No `Starts when:`, so it is simply there - the ruin has
held it for a thousand years and nothing about the crew's arrival changes that.

`relic_piece` is the role every beacon piece carries, and a thing placed at a point wears
that point's roles - so the science route that reveals a piece is written once for all
four ruins, and this file is the only place that says which object is one.

### [the sorting cache](sorting_cache)
---
Relic: voice
Point: 1800, 0, 1500
Roles: voice_treasure
Item: torgoth_salvage
Qty: 3
---
Left behind by whoever emptied the freight hall. Treasure, not plot: taking it is worth
credits and nothing else.

### [the manifest](manifest_place)
---
Relic: voice
Point: 1800, 0, -1500
Roles: voice_clue
Item: clue_manifest
Starts when: reach voice_concourse 900
---
A cargo manifest, still readable. The CLUE - and it does not exist until the crew is
inside, because a clue that can be scooped from outside the ruin is not a discovery, it
is a pickup.
